.env
# The operator's own prompt documents, which supersede the harness defaults the same way `.env`
# supersedes `.env.example`. The `.example` files are documentation and are never loaded.
# Root-anchored so a module or subdirectory prompt file of the same name stays visible.
/SYSTEM.md
/CONTEXT.md
# The tuned ceilings are read by existence and belong to one machine's Docker Desktop allocation.
# compose.limits.yaml.example is the tracked schema; the live file is not. Root-anchored because
# tools/runtime.sh reads it only from the repository root.
/compose.limits.yaml
# Model weights, downloaded on demand into the definition that pins them. Never versioned: the
# tracked artifact is models/<provider>/<id>/weights.lock.json, which names one commit and the
# SHA-256 of every file, so the bytes are reproducible and pointless to store. Pattern-anchored to
# the two-level definition tree, which keeps a project checked out under ./models visible and stops
# this rule from matching anything a contributor might mean to commit.
/models/*/*/weights/
.local/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
container/node_modules/
*.zip

.DS_Store

.agent-state/
.kimi-code/
.playwright-cli/
.serena/
